chapterNumber: 8,
chapterName: "Software Maintenance and Configuration Management",
vivaQuestions: [
{ question: "What is Software Maintenance?", answer: "Sir, software maintenance involves modifying a software product after it has been delivered to correct faults, improve performance, or adapt it to a new environment." },
{ question: "What are the four types of Software Maintenance?", answer: "Yes sir, the four types are Corrective, Adaptive, Perfective, and Preventive maintenance." },
{ question: "What is Corrective Maintenance?", answer: "Sir, corrective maintenance is reactive. It involves fixing bugs and errors that are discovered by users after the software has been deployed." },
{ question: "What is Adaptive Maintenance?", answer: "Sir, adaptive maintenance involves modifying the software to keep it usable in a changing environment, such as a new operating system or database." },
{ question: "What is Perfective Maintenance?", answer: "Sir, perfective maintenance enhances the software by adding new features or functionalities based on new user requirements." },
{ question: "What is Preventive Maintenance?", answer: "Sir, preventive maintenance involves making changes to prevent future problems, like restructuring code to make it more maintainable." },
{ question: "What is Reverse Engineering?", answer: "Sir, reverse engineering is the process of analyzing an existing system to identify its components and extract higher-level design or requirements from the source code." },
{ question: "What is Forward Engineering?", answer: "Sir, forward engineering is the normal software engineering process of moving from high-level requirements to design, and finally to implementation." },
{ question: "What is Re-Engineering?", answer: "Sir, re-engineering is examining and altering an existing software system to reconstitute it in a new form, improving its maintainability without changing its core functionality." },
{ question: "What is SCM?", answer: "Sir, SCM stands for Software Configuration Management. It is the discipline of managing and controlling changes to the software throughout its lifecycle." },
{ question: "What is a Software Configuration Item (SCI)?", answer: "Sir, an SCI is any piece of information created as part of the software engineering process, such as a design document, source code file, or test case." },
{ question: "What is Version Control?", answer: "Sir, version control is the management of multiple revisions or versions of software components, ensuring that developers don't overwrite each other's changes." },
{ question: "What is Change Control?", answer: "Sir, change control is a formal process used to ensure that modifications to a system are evaluated, approved, and tracked before they are implemented." },
{ question: "What is a Baseline in SCM?", answer: "Sir, a baseline is a formally reviewed and approved version of an SCI that serves as a stable foundation for further development." },
{ question: "Why does software require maintenance?", answer: "Sir, software requires maintenance because bugs are found, user needs change, business rules evolve, and underlying hardware or operating systems change." },
{ question: "Which phase consumes the most budget in the SDLC?", answer: "Sir, the maintenance phase consumes the vast majority of the budget, often 60% to 80% of total lifecycle costs." },
{ question: "What is the SCM process?", answer: "Sir, the SCM process includes Identification of objects, Version control, Change control, Configuration auditing, and Status reporting." },
{ question: "What does 'Identification of Objects' mean in SCM?", answer: "Sir, it means uniquely naming and organizing all SCIs so they can be easily tracked and managed by the SCM tools." },
{ question: "What is an example of a Version Control tool?", answer: "Sir, Git, SVN (Subversion), and CVS are common version control tools used in the industry." },
{ question: "Why do we re-engineer legacy systems?", answer: "Sir, legacy systems are often critical to business but difficult to maintain. Re-engineering modernizes the code base making future maintenance easier and cheaper." }
],
